Phase 1 of projects/keeper-housekeeping-upgrade/. Closes the residual housekeeping
gap not covered by the keeper/hound/mole trio:

- check_archive_staleness: flags archive/<bucket>/YYYY-MM-DD/ folders older than
  D-1 (warning) / D-7 (high).
- check_dispatcher_staleness: flags ## Pending entries in dispatcher-inbox.md that
  sat >24h (warning) / >7d (high).
- check_branch_orphan: flags local branches merged to origin/main AND >30d stale;
  emits cap=10 + summary entry past 50.
- check_gitignore_drift: flags expected transient paths missing from .gitignore
  (initial list: dispatcher-outbox.md + scripts/mole-last-sweep.log +
  scripts/archive-clean-last-sweep.log).

All four wired into check_all_products() globals. Colocated regression suite at
mcp/noctusai/tests/test_compliance_hygiene.py (19 tests, 4 test classes). Drive-by
.gitignore patch closes the 3 drift findings this detector emits against current
repo state.

Tracking-shape decision for dispatcher-inbox.md: kept tracked (scaffold body stays
in git, operator churn lives in the gitignored dispatcher-outbox.md).

This is the first methodology rule promoted to Stage 4 of the codification pipeline
with the pipeline explicitly named — see KB § PATTERNS/methodology-codification-pipeline.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
